# Auth and current user (API.md §1). Dev-login works only in Development; the cookie is kept between requests.
# POST /auth/google needs a real Google ID token (copy one from the browser's sign-in request).
# Uses the B1 slot's API port and its own database (recipes_b1).
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5101/api/v1
@fridgeId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Public sign-in configuration
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/config

### Sign in with Google
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/google
Content-Type: application/json
X-Requested-With: fetch

{ "idToken": "paste-a-google-id-token" }

### Sign in with Google: an invalid token → 401 auth.invalid_token
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/google
Content-Type: application/json
X-Requested-With: fetch

{ "idToken": "not-a-token" }

### Sign in without a nickname (dev-login) → onboarding pending
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/dev-login
Content-Type: application/json
X-Requested-With: fetch

{ "email": "nowa@test.local", "nickname": null }

### The signed-in user
GET {{baseUrl}}/me

### Gated while onboarding → 403 user.onboarding_required
GET {{baseUrl}}/recipes

### Is the nickname free?
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/nickname-available?nickname=Łucja

### Pick a nickname
PUT {{baseUrl}}/me/nickname
Content-Type: application/json
X-Requested-With: fetch

{ "nickname": "Łucja" }

### An invalid nickname → 400 nickname.invalid
PUT {{baseUrl}}/me/nickname
Content-Type: application/json
X-Requested-With: fetch

{ "nickname": "a b" }

### Settings (the default fridge must be one of mine, else 404 fridge.not_found)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/me/settings
Content-Type: application/json
X-Requested-With: fetch

{ "liquidUnits": "metric", "defaultFridgeId": "{{fridgeId}}" }

### Product preferences
GET {{baseUrl}}/me/product-preferences

### Log out
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
X-Requested-With: fetch
